---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, SOCIALS } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${SITE.author} and this blog.`}>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>{SITE.author}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{SITE.role}. {SITE.tagline}</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I build AI solutions for a living: retrieval systems, agents that call
      tools, and the evaluation and operations work that turns a promising demo
      into something a team can rely on.
    </p>
    <p>
      This blog is where I write down what actually happened. Most posts start
      as a note to my future self about a decision that looked obvious, went
      sideways in production, and taught me something worth keeping. Expect
      concrete details, small code samples, and opinions I reserve the right to
      revise.
    </p>
    <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Retrieval-augmented generation: chunking, indexing, reranking, and why the boring parts matter most.</li>
      <li>Agents and tool use: designing tools, handling failure, keeping humans in the loop.</li>
      <li>Evaluation: building eval harnesses before shipping features, and measuring what users care about.</li>
      <li>MLOps for LLM systems: observability, cost, latency, and the ops work that keeps everything running.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <p>
      You can find my code on <a href={SOCIALS.github}>GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
